   "derivation": "Dollar stock: 100 until Feb 2020, 80 from Mar 2020, 88 from Dec 2020. The pound falls from 1.25 to 1.00 dollars in Mar 2020. In pounds the stock is 80 throughout (100/1.25, then 80/1.00) until 88 in Dec 2020, so it never falls in pounds, and the Covid window (Jan to Mar 2020) is exactly flat: -20% in dollars, +25% currency, 0.8 x 1.25 = 1. Own view: Nov 2019 to Jan 2021, 14 months, +10% total, three 1-year periods (0%, +10%, +10%), no 3- or 5-year periods, GFC and rate shock not covered. Side by side: the tracker starts Dec 2019, so both are cut to Dec 2019 to Jan 2021 (13 months); the tracker falls 25% from Jan to Mar 2020 (100 to 75, peak is the later of the two 100s) and recovers in May, 4 months underwater; too short for any 36-month rolling correlation. Currency, full history: -12% in dollars (100 to 88), +25% currency, +10% in pounds (0.88 x 1.25 = 1.1). Correlation, volatilities, per-year figures and the 90/10 are produced by Claude's independent reference implementation (validated against every earlier golden file), not hand-worked; the hand-worked facts above were asserted against it."
